From bba40745cf0e83e9c5aa311e6158b54713ef758d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duckfamily <156525766+duckfamily@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 02:32:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] Rename the application to Sealgram

Every identifier Windows or Telegram uses to tell applications apart is now
ours: AppName, AppFile, AppId, the single-instance GUID, the portable folder,
the AppUserModelId, the URL scheme key and the executable name. An official
Telegram Desktop can be installed alongside without the two fighting over a
shared one, which ends in lost data.

AppNameOld points at a folder that has never existed, on purpose: upstream
uses that field to migrate data from an older build of itself, and we must
not go rummaging in another application's directory.

The main menu footer was a hardcoded string with a link to
desktop.telegram.org. It now shows AppName as plain text - this is not that
application, and sending someone there from here would be misleading.
Attribution stays in LICENSE.txt and the executable's file properties.

Strings that name the service rather than the application - Telegram
Premium, Telegram FAQ, Telegram API, "Open Telegram on your phone" - are
deliberately untouched. This is still Telegram's network.

Lang::Instance reapplies the Russian overrides after a cloud language pack
loads, because the downloaded pack would otherwise overwrite them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
